/* What's New: one entry per release, newest first. v matches VERSION in sw.js. s is the one line used in the phone notification
   and the update card; i is the list shown in Settings. Add an entry with every release. Everything after the equals sign, up to the closing semicolon, must stay valid JSON. */
window.TG_CHANGES=[
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-200","d":"2026-11-09","s":"Fixes from a full audit.","i":["Fixed: a split duty (two planned shifts less than 9 hours apart the same day) no longer gets a false you cannot start on time warning.","Fixed: with two drivers, the next shift warning and the rest boxes use the 9 hour rest for two drivers, not reduced rests.","Fixed: when you start a planned shift early, the break advice no longer assumes you finish early too (it could have put a break too soon).","Fixed: running past your planned finish, the break card says you are past your finish instead of no planned shift.","Fixed: the driving since break figure from your tacho is cleared by any full break (or 15 then 30) since, so it can no longer carry into the next day.","Fixed: a change from another device waits while you have a box open that you opened yourself (like Edit shift), so unsaved changes are never closed on you. Boxes the app opens by itself still close after a minute with no taps.","Check against my tacho never turns no-tacho driving into tacho driving."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-199","d":"2026-11-09","s":"Overrun watch: warns before a late finish makes your next shift too early.","i":["During a shift, Today shows your next planned shift and the latest you can finish: for a full 11 hour rest, and at the latest for a reduced 9 hour rest. It turns amber and then red as those times pass.","Phone alerts 30 minutes before each of those times, so you know even with the app closed.","After a shift, if you finished too late for the next planned start, a red warning and an alert give the earliest time you can start, and say to tell your transport office.","Resting: when a full 11 hour rest cannot fit within 24 hours of your shift start, Today no longer shows a Regular 11h time. It says it is not possible, because the rest counts as reduced however long it is."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-198","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Break advice now the same everywhere.","i":["Fixed: when the law needs less break than you planned (for example 30 when you planned 45), the times are now worked out for the break it tells you to take, so taking just that much is always enough. It also checks that taking only 30 does not push your work over 9 hours.","The Plan, the Planned card on Today and the live advice now all come from one set of sums, so they always give the same times for the same shift. Before, a long shift could get different advice in each.","When you plan more break than the law needs, the advice shows what the law needs (for example 30 needed when you planned 45). Your planned break still counts for when the rest falls.","A shift with no plan now shows the same break card, following what you are doing now: the 6 hour clock while working, the driving clock while driving, and how much driving is left as a note.","The Plan form's rules check also gives the 15 then 30 way.","More detail on the split says an early 15 is allowed but makes the window for the 30 tighter, and that Today works it out again once you log the 15."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-197","d":"2026-11-08","s":"The new break card for upcoming shifts too.","i":["Planned today or tomorrow on Today now uses the same break card as a running shift: in one go and split, with the times in big numbers and a timeline from start to finish. The why is still under More detail.","Plan: a shift's details show the same card, with the explanation folded under Why these times.","A shift that needs several breaks lists each one with its latest time.","A break that only fits at one exact time says at 11:00 instead of 11:00–11:00."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-196","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Easier to read break card, and accuracy fixes.","i":["Today: the break card is easier to read. Each break shows its length in big numbers and its times next to it (10:15–10:55, or by 09:45), with a Next by or Due now tag at the top. The two ways (in one go, or split) sit in their own boxes.","Fixed: when your driving clock decides the break, a 45 taken early could leave more than 6 hours of work after it. It now says when the extra 15 goes.","Fixed: when a break is due now, it no longer offers a split with a 30 later.","On POA close to 6 hours of work in a row, Today says to take your break before you work again.","Check against my tacho: a later start no longer leaves the driving total short, and old break entries before the start are tidied away.","Checked by simulating 2,300 whole days following the advice (late, early and split breakers, driving more or less than planned): no rule broken."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-195","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Break needed banners, and Check against my tacho.","i":["Today: a red Break needed now banner when you reach 4h 30m of driving or 6 hours of work in a row, with a Start break button. An amber banner 30 minutes before.","Today: when you stop driving with a lot of driving since your break, it says how much driving is left before your break, or that you cannot drive again until you have had it.","New: Check against my tacho. Put in the start of your day, total driving today, and driving since your last break from your tacho (exact or a good guess). The log is corrected with as little change as possible, and the tacho's driving since break figure is used for your break times.","If no driving is logged after 45 minutes of a tacho shift, Today asks if you have driven.","Welcome back: you can check against your tacho instead of answering what you did.","Breaks: while you are driving, the advice follows your driving clock (a 15 does not restart it), so it never suggests a 30 after you would have passed 4h 30m."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-194","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Breaks: both ways shown, 45 in one go or 15 then 30.","i":["Today: the break advice shows both ways side by side, each worked out to cover you to your finish: 45 in one go (when it has to be) and 15 then 30 (when to take the 15, and the window for the 30). Take whichever happens.","Once you have had a 15, it just shows when the 30 has to be.","If a 45 taken now would mean another 15 later, it says so.","Planned tomorrow and the Plan show both ways too, for example 45 min between 10:15 and 11:00, or 15 about 08:45 then 30 between 10:30 and 15:00.","Break button: says whether now suits a 15 (and when the 30 then goes) or a 45 in one go."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-193","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Clearer break advice, a smarter Break button, and a sync fix.","i":["Fixed: a change made on another device (for example a shift start time changed on a computer) did not reach a phone that had a box left open on screen. Now it waits only while you are using the box; after a minute with no taps it loads the change and says so.","Fixed: syncing no longer depends on each device's clock being right, so a change saved on a device with a slow clock is not missed or overwritten.","Today: the break advice is now a short line with a timeline (the green part is when to take it), and More detail opens the full explanation, including what changes if you finish sooner or run longer.","Today: when resting, the two start times (reduced 9h and regular 11h) are shown side by side, with the explanation under More. The driving since last break bar is hidden while resting.","Break button: says if now is a good time (early, right, or overdue), then asks when the break started: just now, a few minutes ago, or a time you type. A break already over can still be added.","Driving now: the 4h 30m driving limit always comes first in the advice, even if you have driven more than planned.","Plan: the Times vary switch is gone. Planned times are always a guide, and the finish moves with your real start. Break is now Total break, with a note that 45 can be one break or 15 then 30.","Plan: warnings about the rest before a shift now show in yellow (or red when it breaks a rule)."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-192","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Two drivers: you and your co-driver side by side.","i":["With two drivers turned on, Today shows you and your co-driver side by side: what each of you is doing, work in a row and driving since your last break.","It says when your next break together is due and who it is for, for example Break together by 11:00, your co-driver reaches 6 hours of work in a row.","If the one riding is close to 6 hours of work, it says to take the break before they do any work when you stop.","The co-driver figures are worked out from your log: when you drive they ride, when you ride they drive, and other work and breaks are the same for both.","Learn, POA: What Counts and Why: a short note on why two drivers drift apart, and why breaks together keep it simple."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-191","d":"2026-11-08","s":"POA explained, and double manning in the quick shift log.","i":["Learn, Hours Rules: new POA: What Counts and Why, a short table of what POA does to each rule. It pauses your working time but is never a working time break; as the passenger when double manning, the first 45 minutes counts as your driving break only.","Fixed: with two drivers on, the first 45 minutes as co-driver was also counted as a working time break. It now counts for the driving rules only, so the 6 hours and the 30 or 45 minute totals are right.","Today: when you are on POA, or the shift has POA in it, a short note says what it counts as, with a What counts? link.","Log a shift quickly: a two drivers switch. Put in your own driving and your time as the passenger, choose who drove first, and the rest counts as other work. A 15 + 15 break choice, and longer times for POA and other work.","Log a shift quickly can now take a shift of up to 21 hours (two drivers), and says the order is a best guess you can drag into place afterwards.","Questions: new Does POA count as a break?"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-190","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Clearer help text in the i sheets and Settings.","i":["Next Shift From (i) now explains that it allows for your weekly rest as well as your daily rest.","Daily rest (i): removed unclear notes and kept the plain points.","Driving break (i): says that a break taken before you have driven does not count towards it, though it counts for your working time breaks.","Settings: the location check-ins description is in shorter sentences."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-189","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Plainer wording in the Plan.","i":["A rest day for your weekly rest now says so in one sentence, instead of earliest and latest times and a rule check.","Break advice on a planned shift is shorter: when, then one Why line, then how to split it.","Shift details read 45 min break · 4h 30m driving · 11h 15m working time.","Rest before a shift: 12h rest before it. You could start from 04:00, or 02:00 with a reduced rest.","A reduced weekly rest and what you owe are in fewer, shorter sentences.","Free days say You can start at any time and Nothing planned after, so no latest finish.","End Shift: after ending you can start again at a given time, without the confusing extra sentence."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-188","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Today is simpler and clearer: on a break it says what the break counts for, and the wording is plainer.","i":["On a break in the middle of a shift, the top card now says On break, how long so far and what it counts for (for example 15 minutes counted, rest to 45 for a full break). Before, it said Ready to drive or work.","Next shift from now only shows once your shift is over. While you were working it read as if your shift ended then.","The driving advice and Stop Driving By now give the same time.","Under an hour shows in minutes (59 min, not 0h 59m). Limits show as 4h 30m everywhere, not 4.5h, and names match (Driving Since Break, Work Since Break).","Weekly rest: start by Sun 05:00 instead of 5d 21h to start rest, and no more Day 1 of 6.","Breaks: No break yet when you have not had one. The 48 hour average is two short sentences."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-187","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Fix: Today said Ready to drive or work during what your plan needs as your weekly rest.","i":["Today: if your plan has no other break of 24 hours before your weekly rest is due, the time off you are on now is your weekly rest. Today now says Resting, weekly rest, and the earliest you can start (24 hours in, or 45 if your last weekly rest was reduced), instead of Ready.","After 24 hours it says Ready, with a reduced weekly rest, what you would owe, and when it becomes a full one.","The Weekly Rest card now counts your rest from when you stopped, not from now, so it sees the rest you are on."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-186","d":"2026-11-08","s":"Clearer wording for a reduced weekly rest in the Plan.","i":["A reduced weekly rest now says, for example: 38 hours. That is less than the 45 hours a full weekly rest needs, so it counts as a reduced weekly rest (allowed, as it is at least 24 hours). You owe 6h 59m for it. Before, it said That is 24 to 45 hours, which read like a guess."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-185","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Fixes from a check of the latest changes to Edit Shift.","i":["Edit Shift: changing the length of a block that was not a whole number of minutes could freeze the screen. Fixed.","Edit Shift: typing a length and then tapping a button straight away (such as Split it) now works first time.","Edit Shift: saving can never clear entries past the start of your next shift.","Holding − or + by the Started At time no longer brings up the phone's long-press menu."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-184","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Fix: removing every shift of a repeat now ends the repeat, instead of leaving it to carry on after a year.","i":["Plan: ticking every date of a repeat or rota and tapping Remove now ends it there. Before, only the dates the list showed (about a year ahead) were hidden, and the repeat carried on after that.","Repeats removed that way before now are tidied up when the app opens, so they no longer show far-off shifts or affect your rest checks."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-183","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Clearer weekly rest notes in the Plan: dates show the year when it is not this year, long gaps in days, and why a rest has to be your weekly rest.","i":["Dates that are not in this year now show the year, so a date a year away is not mistaken for one coming soon.","Long stretches off are shown in days, not thousands of hours, and owed hours say with nothing planned until a date.","A reduced weekly rest in the Plan now says why it has to be your weekly rest: when your weekly rest must start by (6 days after your last one ended), and how to owe nothing."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-182","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Plan, Weeks now shows each day with what was planned and what you worked.","i":["Plan, Weeks: every day of the week, with the planned shift (times and job) and what you worked (times, job, driving, other work, POA and breaks).","It says how they differed, for example started 10 min late, finished 1h 45m early, and shows not planned, nothing logged or Off where it applies.","The totals include your planned work for the week, and you can look at next week too. Tap a worked shift to change it, or › to open the day."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-181","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Easier splitting and lengths in Edit Shift, a Weeks list in the Plan, and a fix for a false weekly rest warning while working.","i":["Edit Shift: type a block's length in hours and minutes, or use −15, −5, −1, +1, +5 and +15.","Edit Shift: Part of it was something else? now has its own screen. Pick what the other part was, then set one length: for a break, the break part (15, 30, 45 minutes or 1 hour, or any time to the minute), and the other part takes the rest. For example, a break logged as 3h 45m becomes a 19 minute break and 3h 26m of driving.","Plan: a new Weeks view lists every shift you worked in a week, with driving, other work, POA and breaks for each, and the week's totals. Use the arrows to go back a week, and tap a shift to change it.","Fix: while a planned shift was running, the Plan could say your weekly rest would not fit before it was due, because it lost track of when today's shift ends."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-180","d":"2026-11-07","s":"Breaks taken before you drive now show and are explained, and the − and + buttons move in small steps.","i":["Today: the breaks card now shows the breaks taken this shift (for example 17 min), which count towards your working time breaks. It is now called Driving Break, and says that a break taken before you have driven does not count towards the 45 minute driving break. The advice at the top says the same.","Started At: holding − or + now keeps moving one minute at a time, just faster, instead of jumping 5 minutes.","Filling in what you did: the − and + next to Roughly how long? now move 5 minutes at a time, not 15 like the buttons above them."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-179","d":"2026-11-07","s":"The Tacho manual entries reminder now only shows on the shift when you put your card in.","i":["Today: the Tacho manual entries to add reminder only shows during the first tacho shift after no-tacho work, which is the only time the tacho lets you add them. Before, it could stay for up to a week."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-178","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Fixes from a check of the new features.","i":["Edit Shift: an earlier shift can no longer be stretched over the shift before or after it (that could have removed entries from it).","Edit Shift: the Shift started at box now gets the same checks as the other times.","Edit Shift: a piece split off a block keeps that block's job.","Edit Shift: for a no-tacho job, driving is offered as Driving (no tacho), so it does not count towards your tacho driving limits.","Log a shift quickly and What I did now end the shift at its finish when it is your latest shift, so Today does not ask if it ended.","Location check-ins compare with where you were earlier in the shift, not only since your current activity started."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-177","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Today now says when you have had enough breaks, and the help explains how a 15 minute break works for working time.","i":["When your breaks cover the rest of the shift, Today says: You have had enough breaks for this shift.","Work Since Break (i), Learn and the FAQ explain: a 15 minute break stops the 6 hours in a row, but you still need 30 minutes in total over 6 hours of work, or 45 over 9. Some firms ask for 30 minutes before 6 hours to play safe. A 15 never restarts the 4h 30m driving time."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-176","d":"2026-11-06","s":"The planned shift card now says why the break goes where it does, and how splitting it works.","i":["Today, Planned tomorrow: the break window now says why, for example by 11:00 you will have worked 6 hours in a row; before 10:15 you would still have more than 6 hours of work after it.","It also explains splitting: a 15 minute break earlier restarts your 6 hours in a row (and is the first part of a driving break), so the rest can come later.","Once you start the shift, the advice uses your real start and breaks."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-175","d":"2026-11-06","s":"− and + buttons to nudge the start time, and the walkaround is a small link when it is not needed.","i":["Today: − and + either side of the Started At time move it a minute at a time (hold to go faster, then 5 minutes a step). Tap Save to use it.","The walkaround card is now a small Walkaround link at the side when it is not needed: off shift, already done, done elsewhere or not needed. It still opens the checklist. It stays a full card when something needs doing, such as defects or driving with no walkaround."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-174","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Fix: a red 24 hour window warning showed after you had ended your shift in time.","i":["Daily Rest: once your shift has ended, the 24 hour window is checked against when your rest started, not the time now. It now says, for example, Your rest started at 15:15, inside your 24 hour window."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-173","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Edit Shift: split part of a block into another activity. Plan: today shows the shift you worked, not Rest.","i":["Edit Shift: open a block and use Part of it was something else? Pick the activity (for example other work), how long (15m, 30m, 45m, 1h, half, or 5 minutes at a time) and whether it goes at the start or the end. It shows how it will look before you split it.","Splitting the end off what is running now changes what is running (for example POA to driving from 11:30).","Plan: today now shows the shift you worked, such as Worked 05:10 to 15:15, greyed like a past day and still outlined as today, with when you can start again. Before, it said Rest: you need your daily rest."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-172","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Today now lists your shift so you can tap any entry to change it, and asks if your shift ended instead of saying you are ready to drive.","i":["Today: a new This shift list under the activity buttons. Tap any entry to open Edit Shift on it, or tap Edit for the whole shift.","If nothing has been logged for an hour or more and the shift was not ended, Today asks: Did your shift end at 15:15? Before, it counted the time as a break and said you were ready to drive.","Saving in Edit Shift with nothing running now asks if the shift has ended.","The Today's Log button is now Edit shift.","Walkaround done elsewhere is now one short line."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-171","d":"2026-11-06","s":"New Edit Shift screen: your whole shift as a list you can drag into order and change in one place. End Shift uses it too.","i":["Edit Shift shows the whole shift as blocks of driving, other work, POA and breaks, with a coloured bar and totals.","Drag a block by its ≡ handle to change the order. The times follow and the shift keeps its start and length.","Tap a block to change its type, start, end or length (−15, −5, +5, +15), split it, add a block next to it, move it up or down, or delete it.","It checks the rules as you go, and nothing is saved until you tap Save. Undo works after saving.","End Shift opens the same screen with the end time ready. Pick any end time back to your last entry: anything after it is dropped, and it shows the earliest you can start again.","Open it from Today's Log on the Today screen, or Edit shift on any entry in Records."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-170","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Fix: End Shift now lets you pick an end time before something you forgot to stop.","i":["End Shift: if something was still running that started after you really finished (a break or POA you forgot to stop), you can now set the real end time. The running break becomes rest, and POA or work after the end is removed. Before, the time jumped back to when that started.","When End Shift does change your time, it now says why in amber."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-169","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Two drivers: turn on double manning for a shift, and your time riding as co-driver counts as your break.","i":["Today: a new Two drivers this shift switch under the activity buttons (tacho shifts).","With it on, tapping POA asks if you are riding as co-driver or waiting. As co-driver, the first 45 minutes counts as your break as long as you do no work, as GOV.UK allows when the tacho will not let slot 2 change from POA while moving.","Your daily rest window becomes 30 hours (a 9 hour rest within 30 hours of the start), as the two driver rules allow.","Learn: the Two Drivers section explains breaks on the move, and writing any other work on a printout."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-168","d":"2026-11-06","s":"Fix: the Break Taken card no longer says Full break done at the start of a shift.","i":["Today: before you had driven in a shift, the Break Taken card said 45 / 45, Full break done, because the rest before the shift resets your driving time. It now says No break yet this shift, and how much you need, matching the advice at the top."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-167","d":"2026-11-05","s":"Reduced rest start times are now highlighted in yellow in the Plan, and the log preview when you fill in a day is much clearer.","i":["Plan: the earlier start you could make with a reduced 9 hour rest is highlighted in yellow, on free days and on planned shifts, so you can see it is an option.","Free days now show the earliest start, the reduced rest option and the latest finish on separate lines.","How it goes in your log: a coloured bar from start to finish, totals for driving, other work, POA and breaks, and one tidy line per entry with its times and length."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-166","d":"2026-11-05","s":"Free days in the Plan now show the earliest start with a reduced 9 hour rest too, and how many you have left.","i":["Plan: a day with nothing planned now says, for example, Earliest start 04:00 (11 hour rest), or 02:00 with a reduced 9 hour rest (3 of 3 left since your weekly rest). Days with a shift already showed this."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-165","d":"2026-11-04","s":"Fixes: What I did no longer uses the time now as the finish of an earlier shift, and a timer left running is caught and stopped.","i":["What I did on an earlier day starts with the times you logged, not the time now.","If a timer (for example POA) is still running from before entries you have logged after it, TachoGuard asks if you finished when your log ends, and stops it. Before, it carried on counting, so it could ask if you had been on POA all night and make today look like a work day in the Plan.","Undo after saving with What I did, Log a shift quickly or Welcome back now works."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-164","d":"2026-11-03","s":"Location check-ins now look every time you open TachoGuard, and ask if you drove when you have moved a fair way.","i":["With Location Check-ins on, TachoGuard checks roughly where you are each time you open it, and every 10 minutes while it is open.","During a shift, if you have moved 2 miles or more while it has you on other work, POA or a break, it asks: Did you drive? Yes fills in a rough driving time for you to change, and there is also I am driving now, and No (for example as a passenger, or on a ferry).","TachoGuard asks once if you want to turn Location Check-ins on. You can change it any time in Settings, GPS."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-163","d":"2026-11-03","s":"Fix up any day from the Plan with What I did, and turn on Location Check-ins so TachoGuard can tell how far you have driven.","i":["Plan: open a past day, or today, and tap What I did on a planned shift to set it to what really happened: real start and finish, then driving, POA and breaks. It starts from what is already logged, or from the plan, and replaces it. Days with nothing planned have Log what I did this day.","New in Settings, GPS: Location Check-ins (off to start with). TachoGuard notes roughly where you are when you open it, kept on this phone only for 3 days, and never tracks you in the background.","With it on, when it asks what you did it says how far you have moved (for example 28 miles from Depot) and fills in a rough driving time, which you can change.","Saved Places: save your depot, yard or home, then tap where you started when you start a shift late."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-162","d":"2026-11-03","s":"Started late or forgot to log? TachoGuard now asks when you really started and what you did since, and tells you when your next break is due and why.","i":["Starting a shift: say when you really started (as planned, a few minutes ago or a typed time). If it was a while back, turn on what you did since: driving, other work, POA or a break, with rough amounts. Anything left over counts as other work.","It shows how that goes in your log, warns if it breaks a rule, and says when your next break is due and why (for example 4h 30m of driving).","New reminder: if a planned shift has not been started after a set time (30 minutes to start with), your phone asks if you started it. Change it in Settings.","Coming back to the app after a while in a shift, it asks if you were doing the same thing the whole time, and lets you fill in what else you did. Change how long in Settings.","Today's Log has a new Log a shift quickly button: start and finish times, what you did, and the breaks the law needs filled in for you.","The Today card shows when your next break is due even without a planned shift."]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-161","d":"2026-11-01","s":"Each planned shift now shows the rest before it and the earliest you could start, with a full 11 hour rest or a reduced 9 hour one.","i":["Days list and day details: Rest before, how long since your previous shift (logged or planned) ended","The earliest start after a full 11 hour rest, and after a reduced 9 hour rest with how many of your 3 are left since your weekly rest","⚠ when the gap is a reduced rest, or too short to be a daily rest, with the earliest time that would be legal","After a long break it says how many hours off, and when that is your weekly rest"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-160","d":"2026-11-01","s":"Removing a job now also ends its rotas, lists the exact shifts that will go, and can be undone.","i":["Removing a job stops its repeats and rotas from today (ones that had not started yet are deleted) and deletes its single shifts from today on","The box lists the actual upcoming shifts that will go, or says your plan does not change","Undo for 15 seconds puts the job and its shifts back exactly","You cannot remove the job you are on in the middle of a shift: end the shift first","Logged hours keep the job name and colour, and still count towards your limits"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-159","d":"2026-10-29","s":"New Sound switch in Settings, Reminders: turn off the beep the app makes with a reminder while it is open.","i":["Settings, Reminders, Sound: on or off. With it off, reminders still show the box and vibrate","Your choice is saved with your account"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-158","d":"2026-10-29","s":"The small notification icon in your phone's top bar now shows the TachoGuard shield instead of a blank square.","i":["Phone notifications use a white TachoGuard shield as the small top bar icon (Android shows that icon as an outline only, so the full colour app icon showed as a blank square)"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-157","d":"2026-10-28","s":"Info pop-ups and Learn penalties are laid out as clear headings with the explanation underneath.","i":["Every section in an info pop-up has its own heading, with no full stops or colons, and the text underneath starts on its own","The opening part gets an In short heading","Learn, Penalties is laid out the same way, by type of rule"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-156","d":"2026-10-28","s":"Pick any colour for each job, warnings always show ⚠, and Learn now explains penalties and what to ask your employer in place.","i":["Settings, Jobs: pick a colour for each job, or any colour with +","Warnings always carry ⚠, so a colour is never the only sign: days that would mean a reduced rest say ⚠ reduced rest, and shifts with a problem show ⚠","Learn, Penalties now lists the fines and penalties for driving hours, working time and tachograph records, instead of pointing to the info buttons","The FAQ on different reference periods lists the questions to ask each employer"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-155","d":"2026-10-28","s":"Fix: a day off between two weekly rests no longer warns of a reduced weekly rest when a later rest can count instead, and job colours no longer look like warnings.","i":["When no full weekly rest starts in time, the last rest of 24 hours or more that does is counted as your weekly rest, so a shorter one before it is just a long daily rest and nothing extra is owed","Job colours are now blue, purple and pink, so amber only ever means a warning","Today, a planned shift that is over but not logged yet shows as that shift, not as Rest","The weekly rest summary looks past a weekly rest that has already ended before a planned shift"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-154","d":"2026-10-28","s":"A prompt on Today to turn on phone notifications (with a test straight away), and the planned shift cards say clearly which day and times they are for.","i":["Phone notifications are off? A card on Today turns them on, sends a test straight away, and says what went wrong if it could not","On an iPhone it explains how to add TachoGuard to the Home Screen first, and if notifications are blocked it explains how to allow them","Not now hides it for a week, the x for a month","Planned shift cards show the day and times on their own line: Today, Yesterday or the day and date, and the times","When more than two planned shifts need an answer, it says how many more there are"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-153","d":"2026-10-26","s":"Changes to your plan on two phones are now combined shift by shift, and the night work check on Today is right on the days the clocks change.","i":["If you add or remove shifts on two phones before they sync, both sets of changes are kept (before, one phone's changes to the plan could be lost)","Days taken out, and your answers to what happened, are combined the same way","The 00:00 to 04:00 night work check on Today and in your next legal start is right on the days the clocks change"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-152","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Fourth check: a reduced weekly rest that ended with a planned shift you have not logged yet now shows what you owe and where it is made up.","i":["If your rest ended with a planned shift that is not logged yet, the pay back marker, deadline and the rest that makes it up now show, matching the rule check and the summary"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-151","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Third check: the weekly rest summary no longer says you owe hours for time off that does not have to be your weekly rest, and damaged plan entries cannot stop the Plan opening.","i":["Off now for 24 to 45 hours, with a full weekly rest planned in time: the summary calls it a long daily rest with nothing owed, the same as the rule check","Next weekly rest: a full rest in time is used before a reduced one","A damaged shift, repeat or rota is dropped when the app loads instead of stopping the Plan","Removing a shift from its edit screen has Undo, and brings back any days it had pushed out in a clash"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-150","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Second check: planned times are right on the days the clocks change, shifts logged afterwards count their driving, and unlogged shifts are counted until you log them.","i":["Planned shifts on the days the clocks change start and finish at the right time (they were an hour out), and so does the 00:00 to 04:00 night work window","Worked as planned and Different times log the planned driving as driving, so your weekly and fortnight driving limits count it","Worked as planned never logs more break than you planned: if the shift needed more, the rule check shows it","A planned shift with nothing logged counts as worked in the Plan until you say what happened, so the rest after it is not shown as longer than it is","The Today card says when a planned shift is not logged yet","Owed weekly rest only counts as paid back on a full weekly rest or a daily rest, not on another reduced weekly rest","Pay back of reduced weekly rests treats the end of your plan the same way as the rule check"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-149","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Checked and corrected: break advice for long shifts, reduced weekly rest pay back, and breaks in shifts logged afterwards.","i":["Long shifts that need three or more breaks now get a plan for each break, instead of saying the breaks do not fit","Two-break plans keep to the 4h 30m driving limit whichever rule sets the window","When splitting a driving break, the 30 minute part has to be inside the window, not just before its end","A rest of 24 to 45 hours only counts as a reduced weekly rest (and owes hours) when it has to be the weekly rest; otherwise it is shown as a long rest with nothing owed","The Today card shows the break length the shift needs, not just what was planned","Worked as planned logs as many breaks as the shift needs, each in the right place","Break advice on Today uses the planned shift for the job you are on"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-148","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Break advice now counts the breaks you have had, the Today card shows your planned shift and its break, and you can log the breaks you took afterwards.","i":["After a 15 minute break, the advice says how much more you need (for example 30 more, in one go for driving) and when","If you keep driving and will reach 4h 30m sooner than planned, it says take the break by then, and when the next one is due","If your breaks already add up but the rest of the shift is over 6 hours, it says you need one more short break","The Today card shows your next planned shift and when its break goes, before you start","Logging a planned shift afterwards (Different times) asks when each break started and how long it was, for up to 2 breaks","Worked as planned puts the break in the advised window, so the log keeps the rules"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-147","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Month and the repeats calendar show shift times in the 24 hour clock: when each planned shift starts and finishes, and when you started on past days.","i":["Planned shifts in Month show the start (05:00) with the finish (–17:00) under it","Past days show the time you started and the hours you worked","The repeats and rotas calendar uses the same 24 hour times","Times vary shifts have a dashed line instead of the ≈ sign"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-146","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Tacho jobs start with 4h 30m of driving in the shift forms, break advice follows a late start, and Month ticks line up.","i":["Picking a tacho job in a shift, repeat or rota form sets driving to 4h 30m (and the break to 45 minutes) unless you set it yourself","On Today, break advice uses when you really started, your work and driving since your last break, and the driving still planned","For a times vary shift the finish moves with your start, so a late start moves the advice too","It now also says the latest time, and why (6 hours of work or 4h 30m of driving)","In Month the tick, cross or hammer always sits in the same place, with the from time underneath"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-145","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Fix: a rota made before rotas had a start date no longer adds days before the day it was made, or asks what happened on them.","i":["Rotas made on the first day of rotas start on 25 October, not on the Monday of their week 1","The app never asks what happened on a repeat or rota day from before you added it","Rotas that have ended are greyed out in your repeats and rotas"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-144","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Planned shifts say when to take your break so you do not need a second one, the Plan shows where reduced weekly rests are made up, and Month starts on the 1st.","i":["Break advice for each planned shift: the window to take it in, and not before a time, so you are not left needing another break","If one break cannot cover a long shift, it says how to split it and when","On Today, during a shift you planned, it says when to take your break so it lasts to your planned finish","A reduced weekly rest in your plan says how many hours you owe and which rest in your rota makes them up, or how many more hours a rest would need","The rest that makes up owed hours is marked in Days and Month (↺ +9h) and says how long to keep clear","Month shows the month from the 1st, and the rest of its last week"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-143","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Plan page tidied: Days and Month are tabs, one + Add button, rotas can start on any date, and removing shifts can be undone.","i":["Days and Month are now tabs at the top of the Plan","One + Add button at the bottom for a single shift, a repeating shift or a rota, your repeats and rotas, and removing several shifts","This month button removed from Month view","Rotas: pick the date a rota starts, and which week of the rota that is","Ticking shifts to remove now ticks each shift on its own and says if it is a single shift, a repeat or a rota day","When a new repeat or rota clashes with your plan, the shifts that would go are listed, and keeping what is already planned is the first choice","Anything removed from the Plan has an Undo button for 15 seconds","Days left off a repeat or rota come back if the shift that won the clash is removed, and can be brought back from the repeat or rota"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-142","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Repeating shifts and rotas now have their own button on the Plan page.","i":["A Repeating shifts and rotas button sits under Add shift on the Plan page"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-141","d":"2026-10-25","s":"New: rotas for weeks that differ (like week 1 Mon to Thu, week 2 Wed to Sat), and tick shifts to remove them in bulk.","i":["Add a rota from Repeating shifts and rotas: pick 2 to 6 weeks and tick the days for each week","Say which week this week is, and it rolls round from there","Rota days show in the Plan and count in every rules check, and single days can still be changed","Select in the Days list: tick shifts and remove them together, or remove them and every later one","Removing a repeat or rota day now offers this day only, or this one and every later one"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-140","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Repeating shifts: pick how long they run, clashes are caught, and shifts can be marked as times vary.","i":["How long a repeat runs: Forever, 4 weeks, 3 or 6 months, 1 year, or until a date","If a shift or repeat lands on top of another planned shift, you choose which to keep on those days","Times vary: plan rough times as a guide, and the app asks what you really worked at the end"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-139","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Quick shift lengths when adding a shift (+4h to +12h), and dropdown lists are readable in every theme.","i":["Tap +8h, +10h, +12h and so on to set the finish from the start time","Your usual times are still there as one-tap chips","Dropdown boxes and their lists have solid colours, so the text is always readable"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-138","d":"2026-10-25","s":"The shift form's rules check now lists the breaks and rests you need and when, and repeats can be stopped from any date.","i":["Rules check lists the breaks you need and why, when to take them, and your rest before and after the shift","4h 30m of driving or more needs at least 45 minutes of breaks","Removing a repeat: stop from today, stop from a date, remove only the past ones, or remove it all","Month view says now for today","The day chips in the shift form fit on screen"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-137","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Clearer free times, a calendar for repeating shifts, and a 45 minute break when you drive over 4h 30m.","i":["Today says Available now instead of the current time","Free days show the whole time you are free, for example Free from Fri 04:00 until Mon 22:00","Repeating shifts open as a calendar with your repeat days coloured: tap one to change it","With over 4h 30m of driving planned, the break is at least 45 minutes"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-136","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Adding and editing a shift is quicker: tap the day, job, times, break and repeat, and it checks the rules as you go.","i":["Tap a day chip for the next week, or pick another date","Tap your job, and big Start and Finish boxes with your usual times as one-tap chips","Break chips and a Paid switch, and a plus and minus for driving","The shift length, work time and next-day finish show as you type","The rules check runs by itself, and editing has a Remove button"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-135","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Month view shows the earliest you can start on a free day after a shift.","i":["Available days in Month say from 04:00 (for example) when a shift before means you cannot start at midnight"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-134","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Month view now colours each day by what you can do: Working, Available, Available ⚠ or Rest.","i":["Each day in Month is coloured: green Available, amber Available ⚠ (it would mean a reduced rest), red Rest, and your shift times on working days","New key with the same colours","Days from next month are easier to see"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-133","d":"2026-10-25","s":"The Plan's days are simpler: Working, Available or Rest, with a ⚠ when working a day would cut your rest.","i":["A day you could work, but only with a reduced daily or weekly rest, shows ⚠ Available, but... with the reason","Days no longer repeat when your weekly rest starts or ends: tap a day, or see the summary at the top","Available shows how late you can finish when a longer shift would break a rule"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-132","d":"2026-10-25","s":"The Plan now lists your days one by one: Working, Available or Rest, with how each day fits your weekly rest.","i":["New Days view: every day says Working (your shift), Available (with from or until times) or Rest (with the reason)","A second line shows when your weekly rest starts or ends, and which days are weekly rest days","Month view uses the same words: Available and Rest","Summary at the top says if you are off now and when your next weekly rest is"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-131","d":"2026-10-25","s":"The Plan is easier to read: your time off is shown as days off, with a plain summary at the top.","i":["Time off of 24 hours or more shows across the days it covers: Off from, Day off, Back. Green is a full weekly rest, amber a reduced one","A summary at the top says if you are off now, until when, and when your next weekly rest is in your plan","Warnings only show when your plan does not leave room for a weekly rest, with Rest due on the day it must start","Blue days are your working days before the next weekly rest","Free days say From 04:00 instead of codes, and the key is rewritten"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-130","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Plan's weekly rest labels now say what they mean: 137h off, Rest from 17:00, Rest by 09:00.","i":["Calendar labels read 137h off (your rest before these 6 days), Rest from (earliest start of your next weekly rest) and Rest by (the latest start)","Tapping the day explains each one, and says when your plan already has the rest covered"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-129","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Plan shows when your next weekly rest is due, even while you are on days off.","i":["A line above the calendar says when your next weekly rest must start and whether your plan leaves room for it","While you are on a weekly rest, the Plan works out the next 6 days from your next planned shift","Shifts in the first days of next month now show on this month's calendar"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-128","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Planned shifts now show when to take your breaks, and a break can be marked as paid.","i":["Each planned shift shows the window for its break so you never work more than 6 hours in a row","Tacho shifts with over 4h 30m of driving show when the driving break is due","Breaks are just called breaks, with a paid tick for your own records (paid or unpaid, a break is never working time)"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-127","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Plan now tells you the latest you can finish if you start a free day late, and why.","i":["A free day says the latest you can finish if you start at the earliest time, with the reason in plain words","A day that is fine says which shift was checked in one line","A day you cannot work says that even a short shift would break the rule, and which one"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-126","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Phones are told when an update goes live, with what changed. See What's New in Settings.","i":["When a new version goes live, phones with notifications on get a message saying what changed","The update card shows what is new","New What's New list in Settings"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-125","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Removing a job keeps its name on your logged hours and clears its future shifts.","i":["A removed job keeps its name on the hours you logged for it","Removing a job asks first and removes its planned and repeating shifts from today on","The Log shows which job each entry was for"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-124","d":"2026-10-25","s":"A card now tells you when a new version is ready, with an Update now button.","i":["Update card at the top of every tab when a new version is live","\"Drivers' hours\" removed from the header"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-123","d":"2026-10-25","s":"Plan no longer marks a free day as unavailable because of a night-time test shift.","i":["A free day is only shown as unavailable if no sensible shift fits","If a shorter shift fits, the day says which longer one would not and why"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-122","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Plan checks the 48 hour average for each company's own reference period.","i":["Plan checks the 48 hour average against every company's reference period and names the company"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-121","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Headings use one style across the app.","i":["Headings, titles and card names use the same capital letters style"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-120","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Tighter account storage limits and a clearer message if a save is ever refused.","i":["Account and walkaround check size limits","Defect notes capped at 500 characters","Clearer message if your account is full"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-119","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Layout fixes for small screens and dark mode.","i":["Reset Day readable in dark mode","Plan day labels no longer cut off","Started At fits small phones","Break Check asks once per launch"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-118","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Rule wording checked against gov.uk, and leave counts 48 hours a week.","i":["Wording corrected for weekly rests abroad, driver cards, two-driver crews and several signs","A whole week of leave counts as 48 hours in your 48 hour average","Add leave taken after you started using the app, in Records, Hours"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-117","d":"2026-10-24","s":"Fixes to times around the clock change, editing and start-of-day screens.","i":["Times around the clock change land on the right hour","Started At asks before replacing entries, with Undo","Last Day Check applies your answers and has Cancel","Repeating shift edits replace the old pattern"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-116","d":"2026-10-23","s":"Today and the start check use one full list of driving and working time rules.","i":["Adds the 24 hour window, 3 reduced rests, 60 hour week, night work and 10 hour days to the countdown","Working time break after 6 hours in a row","The Break button no longer locks"]},
{"v":"tg-2026-10-23-115","d":"2026-10-23","s":"Safer syncing between phones and safer sign-in links.","i":["Changes made on two phones are combined instead of overwritten","Sign-in links ask you to confirm","Damaged saved data no longer stops the app opening"]}
];
